  "question": {
    "text": "Let the normal at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> on the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;pass through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the tangent at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;to the parabola intersects its directrix at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>, then the ordinate of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0062_5ca174ac30ab.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;comparing with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now normal at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>Now this normal is passing through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now solving above equation&nbsp;we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>So tangent at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>putting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>Now tangent is intersecting&nbsp;at directrix which is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So point of intersection is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
}